# SHA-256 checksums for the distro-independent tarballs the install scripts
# download.
#
# Native .deb/.rpm packages (pe-utils, edge-proxy, the CNI plugin, kubelet,
# pe-terminal) are NOT listed here - they come from the Izuma package
# repository (see lib/distro.sh's setup_izuma_repo), whose signed repo
# metadata (repo_gpgcheck) is verified by dnf/apt themselves. Only the plain
# tarballs below still need a pinned hash in this file.
#
# The scripts verify each tarball download against this file so that a
# tampered or truncated artifact is rejected before its install.sh is
# executed as root.
#
# This file is the trust anchor, so it must reach the host through a channel you
# trust (git over HTTPS, a signed release), not alongside the tarballs.
#
# Regenerate after publishing a new tarball:
#   sha256sum <files> >> scripts/checksums.sha256
#
# Format is sha256sum(1)'s: <hash>  <basename>

# --- Service tarballs (distribution independent) ----------------------------
# These are extracted and their install.sh is run with sudo, so verifying them
# matters more than the packages: a swapped tarball is arbitrary root code.
1c55ac07666de0ef53a816fbe030939a093eb64ec96b0ec74fad4350ab1c7411  kubelet.tar.gz
892deeb5130e86aa1d19abc49ed6300dbd54974302db862bc0ead0a9b20d60a3  kube-router_1_2_0_1.tar.gz
